{
  "_comment": [
    "One registry entity per seeded device, and the reason is Home Assistant's own cleanup.",
    "",
    "helpers/device_registry.async_cleanup removes every device that is referenced by neither",
    "a live config entry nor an entity registry entry. The seeded devices carry no config",
    "entry — nothing in this fixture could give them a real one — so they were orphans, and HA",
    "deleted them the first time the debounced cleanup fired (CLEANUP_DELAY = 10s, and on every",
    "restart). The device-rename case therefore passed or failed depending on how long the tier",
    "took to reach it, which is worse than failing: it went green while the shape it tests was",
    "being removed underneath it.",
    "",
    "These two rows are the anchor. Their platform is `demo`, deliberately not the fixture's",
    "custom component, so they cannot be mistaken for entities `cc show` should attribute.",
    "",
    "Side effect, recorded rather than discovered later: `demo` is not set up, so HA publishes",
    "each of these as a RESTORED ghost — state `unavailable`, attribute `restored: true`. That",
    "is a real shape a real instance has (the reference instance carries 37 of them) and the rig",
    "had none.",
    "",
    "Key set and minor_version taken from the loader in the image",
    "(helpers/entity_registry.py, _async_load), not guessed: HA indexes these keys directly and",
    "KeyErrors on a missing one."
  ],
